{% liquid
  assign slide_blocks = section.blocks | where: 'type', 'slide'
  assign trust_blocks = section.blocks | where: 'type', 'trust_item'
%}

{% style %}
  /* The wave divider's gradient (see the SVG at the end of this file)
     approximates the true color of Shop by Category's background along
     the seam line, which depends on that section's width-to-height
     ratio — a much narrower, differently-proportioned box on mobile, so
     the ramp reaches nowhere near as far into the gradient there as it
     does on desktop before hitting the right edge. Without this, the
     mobile wave carried the desktop ramp's colors straight through and
     visibly mismatched the actual section again at this breakpoint. */
  @media (max-width: 480px) {
    #heroDividerGradient-{{ section.id }} stop:nth-child(2) {
      stop-color: #e3d8f4;
    }
    #heroDividerGradient-{{ section.id }} stop:nth-child(3) {
      stop-color: #dbccf1;
    }
  }
{% endstyle %}

<div class="j-hero-band full-width">

  <div
    class="j-hero-slideshow"
    data-autoplay="3000"
    role="region"
    aria-roledescription="carousel"
    aria-label="Hero"
  >

    {%- comment -%}
      The first slide is the LCP image when the hero opens the page, so it
      gets fetchpriority="high". Placed lower down it stays at normal
      priority. section.index is nil in the editor, which keeps "high".
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- liquid
      assign hero_priority = 'high'
      if section.index > 1
        assign hero_priority = 'auto'
      endif
    -%}

    <div class="j-hero-slideshow__track">
      {% for block in slide_blocks %}
        <div
          class="j-hero j-hero-slideshow__slide{% if forloop.first %} is-active{% endif %}"
          data-slide-index="{{ forloop.index0 }}"
          {% unless forloop.first %}aria-hidden="true" inert{% endunless %}
          {{ block.shopify_attributes }}
        >

          <div class="j-hero__content">

            {% if block.settings.badge != blank %}
              <span class="j-hero__badge">{{ block.settings.badge }}</span>
            {% endif %}

            <h1>
              {{ block.settings.heading }}
              <span class="j-hero__highlight">{{ block.settings.highlight_heading }}</span>
            </h1>

            <p>{{ block.settings.description }}</p>

            <div class="j-hero__buttons">
              <a
                href="{{ block.settings.button_link | default: routes.all_products_collection_url }}"
                class="j-button"
              >
                {{ block.settings.button_label }}
              </a>

              <a
                href="{{ block.settings.secondary_link | default: routes.all_products_collection_url }}"
                class="j-button j-button-outline"
              >
                {{ block.settings.secondary_label }}
              </a>
            </div>

            {% render 'hero-trust', trust_blocks: trust_blocks %}

          </div>

          {% comment %}
            aria-hidden — this is purely decorative background media (the
            actual slide content — heading, description, CTA — is marked
            up separately as real text below), and it's always muted with
            no spoken audio, so a captions track wouldn't convey anything
            a screen reader user needs. Hiding it from assistive tech
            entirely is the correct treatment here, rather than adding a
            captions track with nothing meaningful to caption.
          {% endcomment %}
          <div class="j-hero__image" aria-hidden="true">

            {% if block.settings.video %}

              {% comment %}
                Only the first/active slide's video is eager + autoplaying.
                Other slides get their <source> deferred the same way
                images are (data-src, hydrated on idle) — a video file is
                far heavier than an image, so downloading N of them
                upfront for slides the visitor may never reach is worse
                here than it ever was for photos. hero-slideshow.js starts
                playback only once a slide actually becomes active, and
                pauses it again when the slide is left, so at most one
                hero video is ever playing at a time.
              {% endcomment %}

              {% comment %}
                video_tag lists every rendition Shopify generated, and a
                browser plays the first source it supports — normally the
                largest mp4 (often 1080p, several MB per slide) for a hero
                whose box is at most ~560px wide on desktop and full-width
                but only ~412px on a phone. Picking the largest mp4 at or
                below 720p ourselves keeps the same look at a fraction of
                the bytes (and decode work). Falls back to plain video_tag
                if the file has no mp4 rendition in range.
              {% endcomment %}
              {% liquid
                assign hero_video = block.settings.video
                assign hero_source = nil
                for source in hero_video.sources
                  if source.format == 'mp4' and source.height <= 720
                    if hero_source == nil or source.height > hero_source.height
                      assign hero_source = source
                    endif
                  endif
                endfor
              %}

              {% if forloop.first %}
                {% comment %}
                  The homepage's LCP element. A <video> can't be made an
                  early, high-priority LCP on its own: fetchpriority isn't a
                  valid attribute on <video>, and browsers start video
                  downloads late and at low priority — Lighthouse measured
                  ~5.5s before this video's request even began. Painting
                  its first frame as a real <img> (fetchpriority=high, in
                  the initial HTML) makes that the LCP instead. The video
                  sits on top at opacity 0 and fades in once it's actually
                  playing (see .j-hero__video--over-poster in hero.css and
                  hero-slideshow.js); at the same size, that later paint
                  doesn't replace the image as LCP.
                {% endcomment %}
                {% comment %}
                  sizes: a video frame is landscape, but on phones the hero
                  is a tall portrait box, so object-fit: cover draws the
                  frame roughly twice the viewport width (sides cropped).
                  With a plain 100vw the browser fetched a frame smaller
                  than it's actually drawn — Chrome discounts an upscaled
                  image's LCP size, so the full-resolution video replaced
                  it as LCP the moment it started playing.

                  widths go up to 1800 for the same reason on desktop: Chrome
                  never credits an image with more pixels than its file has,
                  so a 1200px-wide frame stretched across a wider hero
                  counted as smaller than the 720p video over it, and LCP
                  flipped to the video on some runs.
                {% endcomment %}
                {% if hero_video.preview_image %}
                  {{
                    hero_video.preview_image
                    | image_url: width: 1800, format: 'webp'
                    | image_tag:
                      loading: 'eager',
                      fetchpriority: hero_priority,
                      widths: '480, 760, 1000, 1200, 1500, 1800',
                      sizes: '(max-width: 749px) 200vw, 100vw',
                      class: 'j-hero__img',
                      alt: ''
                  }}
                {% endif %}
                {% if hero_source %}
                  <video class="j-hero__video j-hero__video--over-poster"
                    preload="metadata"
                    muted="muted"
                    loop="loop"
                    playsinline="true"
                    autoplay="autoplay"
                  ><source src="{{ hero_source.url }}" type="{{ hero_source.mime_type }}"></video>
                {% else %}
                  {{
                    block.settings.video
                    | video_tag:
                      image_size: '1200x',
                      class: 'j-hero__video j-hero__video--over-poster',
                      muted: true,
                      loop: true,
                      playsinline: true,
                      autoplay: true
                  }}
                {% endif %}
              {% else %}
                {% comment %}
                  Same structure as the first slide: the video's first frame as
                  a real <img>, with the video on top (1px smaller, hidden until
                  it plays). The poster used to be a poster="" attribute, which
                  the browser fetched for every slide at page load; as an <img>
                  it goes through the same data-src deferral as image slides.
                  It also keeps a later slide's video from ever outranking the
                  first slide's image as the page's LCP element.
                {% endcomment %}
                {% capture deferred_hero_video %}
                  {% if hero_video.preview_image %}
                    {{
                      hero_video.preview_image
                      | image_url: width: 1800, format: 'webp'
                      | image_tag:
                        widths: '480, 760, 1000, 1200, 1500, 1800',
                        sizes: '(max-width: 749px) 200vw, 100vw',
                        class: 'j-hero__img',
                        alt: ''
                    }}
                  {% endif %}
                  {% if hero_source %}
                    <video class="j-hero__video j-hero__video--over-poster"
                      preload="metadata"
                      muted="muted"
                      loop="loop"
                      playsinline="true"
                    ><source src="{{ hero_source.url }}" type="{{ hero_source.mime_type }}"></video>
                  {% else %}
                    {{
                      block.settings.video
                      | video_tag:
                        image_size: '1200x',
                        class: 'j-hero__video j-hero__video--over-poster',
                        muted: true,
                        loop: true,
                        playsinline: true
                    }}
                  {% endif %}
                {% endcapture %}
                {{ deferred_hero_video | replace: ' src=', ' data-src=' | replace: ' srcset=', ' data-srcset=' | replace: ' poster=', ' data-poster=' }}
              {% endif %}

            {% elsif block.settings.image %}
              {% if forloop.first %}
                {% assign img_alt = block.settings.heading | default: shop.name %}
                {{
                  block.settings.image
                  | image_url: width: 1200, format: 'webp'
                  | image_tag:
                    loading: 'eager',
                    fetchpriority: hero_priority,
                    widths: '360, 480, 600, 760, 1000, 1200',
                    sizes: '100vw',
                    class: 'j-hero__img',
                    alt: img_alt
                }}
              {% else %}
                {% comment %}
                  Every slide sits at position: absolute; inset: 0 from
                  first paint (see hero.css), all overlapping the same
                  viewport-visible box the active slide occupies — so
                  loading="lazy" never defers them; the browser considers
                  them "in view" immediately and fetches all N slide images
                  upfront. Withholding src/srcset (via data-src/data-srcset)
                  until hero-slideshow.js hydrates them on idle avoids
                  downloading slides the visitor may never scroll to.
                {% endcomment %}
                {% capture deferred_hero_image %}
                  {% assign img_alt = block.settings.heading | default: shop.name %}
                  {{
                    block.settings.image
                    | image_url: width: 1200, format: 'webp'
                    | image_tag:
                      widths: '360, 480, 600, 760, 1000, 1200',
                      sizes: '100vw',
                      class: 'j-hero__img',
                      alt: img_alt
                  }}
                {% endcapture %}
                {{ deferred_hero_image | replace: ' src=', ' data-src=' | replace: ' srcset=', ' data-srcset=' }}
              {% endif %}
            {% else %}
              <div class="j-hero__placeholder">
                {{ 'lifestyle-1' | placeholder_svg_tag: 'j-hero__placeholder-svg' }}
              </div>
            {% endif %}

          </div>

          {% if slide_blocks.size > 1 %}
            <div class="j-hero-slideshow__arrows">
              <button
                type="button"
                class="j-hero-slideshow__arrow j-hero-slideshow__arrow--prev"
                aria-label="{{ 'general.pagination.prev' | t }}"
              >
                <svg viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none" aria-hidden="true">
                  <path d="M12.5 15 7.5 10l5-5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
                </svg>
              </button>

              <button
                type="button"
                class="j-hero-slideshow__arrow j-hero-slideshow__arrow--next"
                aria-label="{{ 'general.pagination.next' | t }}"
              >
                <svg viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none" aria-hidden="true">
                  <path d="M7.5 5 12.5 10l-5 5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
                </svg>
              </button>
            </div>
          {% endif %}

        </div>
      {% endfor %}
    </div>

  </div>

  {% comment %}
    Curved divider into Shop by Category — the hero (a dark video/photo)
    used to cut off abruptly into that section's light purple gradient
    background with a hard flat seam. This wave shape, filled with a
    color sampled from that gradient's lighter stop, sits on top of the
    hero's own bottom edge so it reads as the next section flowing up
    into it, instead of two unrelated blocks just stacked on top of each
    other. Purely decorative (aria-hidden) and never intercepts clicks
    on the arrows/content above it.
  {% endcomment %}
  <svg class="j-hero-band__divider" viewBox="0 0 1440 80" preserveAspectRatio="none" aria-hidden="true">
    {% comment %}
      Reusing the section's own 0%/50%/100% stops at the same 0°→100%
      corner angle (the previous version of this) looked mismatched
      because that angle is only correct for a box shaped like this tiny
      80px-tall strip — for Shop by Category's actual, much taller box,
      a true CSS 135deg gradient's color at any point along this exact
      seam line works out to a *horizontal-only* ramp from stop 0 at the
      left edge to roughly the midpoint between stop 1 and stop 2 at the
      right edge (derived from the gradient-line-length formula CSS uses
      for angled gradients, assuming a plausible section height) — not a
      diagonal ramp reaching all the way to stop 2. This mirrors that
      instead, so the seam's colors actually line up with what the
      section itself shows along its own top edge.
    {% endcomment %}
    <defs>
      <linearGradient id="heroDividerGradient-{{ section.id }}" x1="0%" y1="0%" x2="100%" y2="0%">
        <stop offset="0%" stop-color="#f3effa"/>
        <stop offset="67%" stop-color="#d9c9f0"/>
        <stop offset="100%" stop-color="#e3d5f4"/>
      </linearGradient>
    </defs>
    {% comment %}
      A single gentle S-curve, not the previous double-hump path — that
      one's control points (y=0 and y=90 against an 80-tall viewBox)
      overshot the divider's own bounds, so the curve pinched to a sharp
      point at the top and let the hero image poke through above it as a
      hard diagonal seam instead of a smooth wave. Every point here stays
      well inside 0–80, so the fill covers the full band edge to edge.
    {% endcomment %}
    <path d="M0,52 C240,24 480,24 720,46 C960,68 1200,68 1440,42 L1440,80 L0,80 Z" fill="url(#heroDividerGradient-{{ section.id }})"/>
  </svg>

</div>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Slideshow",
  "settings": [],
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "slide",
      "name": "Slide",
      "settings": [
        {
          "type": "image_picker",
          "id": "image",
          "label": "Image",
          "info": "Ignored if a video is set below."
        },
        {
          "type": "video",
          "id": "video",
          "label": "Video",
          "info": "Plays muted and looping. Overrides the image when set."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "badge",
          "label": "Badge",
          "default": "Premium Lifestyle Collection"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "heading",
          "label": "Heading",
          "default": "Discover Your"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "highlight_heading",
          "label": "Highlighted Heading",
          "default": "Next Favorite"
        },
        {
          "type": "textarea",
          "id": "description",
          "label": "Description",
          "default": "Carefully selected products crafted for modern living. Simple. Elegant. Timeless."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "button_label",
          "label": "Primary button label",
          "default": "Shop Now"
        },
        {
          "type": "url",
          "id": "button_link",
          "label": "Primary button link"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "secondary_label",
          "label": "Secondary button label",
          "default": "Explore"
        },
        {
          "type": "url",
          "id": "secondary_link",
          "label": "Secondary button link"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "trust_item",
      "name": "Trust item",
      "settings": [
        {
          "type": "select",
          "id": "icon",
          "label": "Icon",
          "options": [
            { "value": "shipping", "label": "Shipping" },
            { "value": "returns", "label": "Returns" },
            { "value": "secure", "label": "Secure" },
            { "value": "quality", "label": "Quality" }
          ],
          "default": "shipping"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "text",
          "label": "Text",
          "default": "Free Shipping"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "max_blocks": 7,
  "presets": [
    {
      "name": "Slideshow",
      "blocks": [
        { "type": "slide" },
        {
          "type": "trust_item",
          "settings": { "icon": "shipping", "text": "Free Shipping" }
        },
        {
          "type": "trust_item",
          "settings": { "icon": "returns", "text": "Easy Returns" }
        },
        {
          "type": "trust_item",
          "settings": { "icon": "secure", "text": "Secure Checkout" }
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
